M05_DEAD6_MiniGunner (Deadeye) completes objective 502 only when the
non-key conversation M05_CON013 (action 300004) ends with ENDED. Poked()
started it before Monitor_Conversation, so a start refused by a playing key
conversation (M05_CON003-008/014/037/038, e.g. the Inn radio M05_CON004)
stopped with INTERRUPTED before any monitor existed. An INTERRUPTED end
(player left the conversation range) was also ignored. Either way poke_id
was 3 and conversation stayed true, so Deadeye could never be poked again
and 502 stayed pending for the rest of the mission (retail behaviour).
Register the monitor (and the poke state) before starting, and re-arm the
poke on an INTERRUPTED end of 300004. The ENDED path is unchanged.

--- a/Mission05.cpp
+++ b/Mission05.cpp
@@ -1274,6 +1274,14 @@
 			conversation = false;
 			
 		}
+		// Vita: an interrupted rescue talk re-arms the poke instead of
+		// leaving 502 pending forever.
+		if(action_id == 300004 && reason == ACTION_COMPLETE_CONVERSATION_INTERRUPTED && poke_id == 3)
+		{
+			conversation = false;
+			poke_id = 1;
+			Commands->Enable_HUD_Pokable_Indicator( obj, true );
+		}
 		if(action_id == 300004 && reason == ACTION_COMPLETE_CONVERSATION_ENDED)
 		{
 			Commands->Set_Innate_Is_Stationary(obj, false);
@@ -1373,11 +1381,12 @@
 					int conv_id = Commands->Create_Conversation (conv_name, 100.0f, 200.0f, false);
 					Commands->Join_Conversation(STAR, conv_id, false, true);
 					Commands->Join_Conversation(obj, conv_id, false, true);
-					Commands->Start_Conversation (conv_id, 300004);
-					Commands->Monitor_Conversation (obj, conv_id);
+					// Vita: monitor before starting, so a start refused by a
+					// playing key conversation still reports INTERRUPTED.
 					Commands->Enable_HUD_Pokable_Indicator( obj, false );
-
 					poke_id = 3;
+					Commands->Monitor_Conversation (obj, conv_id);
+					Commands->Start_Conversation (conv_id, 300004);
 		
 				}
 			break;
